-- documented guess: borrowed from 3.0.4.2
-- 3.0 gear batch 1b-costumes (inventory report section 7). Retail 3.0 content only.
-- Base: the 1.2 database with 2026-10-21-gear-3.0-batch-1a.sql applied (patches run
--   in file-name order), so batch 1a items and their synthesized look ids are present.
-- Selection: item id absent from 1.2 and batch 1a and below 8,000,000; not an
--   emulator-custom Dawnsdrop item (set id >= 9,000,001 or item id 34936..34984);
--   item level <= 62 (the Eanad power line); costume only (category 10/173 or armor
--   slot 31, category not 94/96/100); no item proc, no set proc, no set bonus unit
--   attribute above 186, no 3.0-only use skill; a look for each of the four playable
--   races, at least one playable look path absent from the 1.2 pak (the batch 1a
--   complement) and every playable look path present in the 3.0.4.2 pak (the overlay
--   source). Dwarf/Warborn look paths are imported as data-only item_assets rows.
-- Selected: 313 costumes = 313 items.
-- Skipped candidates: above_eanad 5, custom_dawnsdrop_item 20, custom_dawnsdrop_set 84, custom_id_ge_8m 2270, new_use_skill 10, no_four_race_art 24, outside_batch_family 7147, playable_art_missing_from_3_0 220.
-- Looks: 1874 distinct paths = 1249 playable-race + 625 Dwarf/Warborn + 0 race-neutral.
--   34 playable paths already exist in the 1.2 pak and are reused; 1215 are new in the 3.0 chains, 907 of them are imported primary looks and carried by the overlay (the rest are 3.0 asset2_id secondary looks, which 1.2 cannot store).
--   Changed-shared-file rule: the overlay only ADDS files. The five direct look paths whose 3.0 bytes differ from 1.2 (the four female award001 .chr files and nu_m_sk_lucius001.chr) keep the 1.2 file: they are the same costume models (lucius001 is the 1.2 item 16066 art), so the imported costumes render that outfit and no existing 1.2 art changes. Changed closure materials/textures are skipped by the overlay tool's --new-only and listed in the manifest.
-- Overlay input: 907 new playable-race look paths + 200 new item icons; cargo xtask overlay-pak --closure --new-only --exclude-path /characters/dwarf/ --exclude-path /characters/warborn/ adds their materials/textures/models and enforces the add-only, four-race rule.
-- Rows inserted: armor_assets 119, buffs 4, craft_effects 1, craft_materials 34, craft_products 19, crafts 19, dyeable_items 76, effects 1, icons 199, item_armor_assets 1439, item_armors 313, item_assets 1392, items 315, localized_texts 735, skill_effects 1, skills 1, tagged_buffs 4, unit_modifiers 4.
-- Keyed-child checks: localized_texts by (tbl_name, tbl_column_name, idx); item_armors/item_weapons/item_accessories and item_grade_enchanting_supports, item_enchanting_gems, dyeable_items, item_body_parts, item_summon_mates, item_summon_slaves, item_backpacks by item_id.
--   unit_modifiers (owner_id), craft_products/craft_materials (craft_id), tagged_buffs, skill_modifiers and equip_item_set_bonuses are multi-row children; checked, none had an existing row for the imported parents.
-- Idempotent: every INSERT is guarded by NOT EXISTS on its id, every UPDATE is guarded by the row's natural key (item_id or the localized_texts key) and writes the same values again, so a rerun is a no-op.
